   "final": "9 customers, 26,546 orders (id and `#name`), 37,773 order lines, 49 variants |\n| Amazon | 38,264 orders, 43,513 order lines, 49 FBA inbound shipments, 25 listings (seller SKU, ASIN, FNSKU) |\n| 3PL | 49 item codes, 29 receipts, 146 receipt lines, 37,331 outbound lines |\n| QuickBooks | 11 vendors |\n| Supplier PDFs | 135 files; the 89 factory PIs and CIs were read for the product crosswalk |\n\nLines carry `core/part_of` and `line/sku`. Receipts carry `receipt/po`. Shopify orders carry `order/customer`.\n\n## Crosswalk\nThere are 49 product hubs, each holding our SKU code.\n\n| Link | Hubs | Tier |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shopify variant, UPC, 3PL item code | 49 | exact, via the barcode (confidence 1) |\n| `sku/code` | 43 | exact (1) |\n| `sku/code` | 6 | normalized (0.9); the Shopify spelling breaks the pattern |\n| Amazon seller SKU, ASIN, FNSKU | 14 | exact (1) |\n| Amazon seller SKU, ASIN, FNSKU | 11 | normalized (0.9); `-FBA` suffix or a malformed Shopify SKU |\n| Factory item code, supplier, HS code | 49 | corroborated (0.7); the factory description equals our title plus variant |\n| QuickBooks vendor \u2194 supplier | 8 suppliers | normalized (0.9); email domain plus legal name |\n\n- **Amazon:** 24 of the 49 hubs have no Amazon listing, because the export has only 25 listings.\n- **QuickBooks:** the other 3 vendors (forwarder, broker, 3PL) are indexed under their vendor name alone.\n- **Malformed Shopify SKUs:** `AH-CTB-16-LRG`, `AHUTN0017NAT`, `AH-TRY-18-NAT`, `ah-btl-0020-blk`, `AH-JAR-22-STL` and `AH-TPT-23-CLR`. The hub uses the pattern-conforming spelling.\n- **3PL Client SKU:** its typos (`BKL`, `WTH`, `SVL`, `HFL`, `BMA`) and blanks were used as evidence only. The match is by UPC.\n\n## Attributes registered\nNone. The installed vocabulary already covered every identifier and join key.\n\n## Duplicate customers\nI marked 154 accounts with `core/same_as`, in 151 groups (148 pairs and 3 groups of three).\n- **84 by normalized mailbox** (plus-alias dropped), confidence 0.9.\n- **70 by same full name and postal address**, confidence 0.7. I only used addresses where the shipping name equals the customer's own name.\n- **Review:** all 154 pairs have matching first and last names. No account has more than 2 others pointing at it, and there are no chains.\n\n## Checks\n- **Counts:** every kind of record matches the distinct IDs in its source.\n- **Bare join-key records:** the only ones are 26 `po/number` records, named by receipts and not yet ingested. All are well-formed (`PO-YYYY-NNNN`). 10 receipts have a blank PO reference, so I wrote no ref for them.\n\n## Terms the sources disagree on\n- **\"SKU\":**\n  - Shopify's is hand-typed and sometimes malformed.\n  - Amazon's is a listing code with an `-FBA` suffix.\n  - The 3PL has its own \"Item Code\" and a hand-typed \"Client SKU\" that is wrong or blank on several items.\n  - I kept Amazon's spelling in `amazon/seller_sku`. Shopify's and the 3PL's variants were used as evidence only.\n- **Stock figures:**\n  - Shopify's `inventoryQuantity` matches the 3PL's Available.\n  - The 3PL's On Hand is a different figure that includes allocated units.\n  - Amazon splits stock into fulfillable, unsellable and reserved.\n  - These values stay in their sources, so I stored no attribute for them.\n\n## Left out\n- **`quickbooks/transaction_list_by_vendor.csv`:** it's the general ledger, which is never indexed.\n- **`email/ops_inbox.mbox` and the 8 WeChat chats:** these belong to the ingestion skill. The 46 other PDFs (the 3PL's and the inspection reports) are in the same position.\n\n## For you to decide\n1. The 3PL receipts name a container (`TCLU...`) and an ASN, but the vocabulary has no `receipt/shipment` join. Linking receipts to shipments would need one to be registered, plus ingested shipments to point at.\n2. The 70 name-and-address matches are weaker (0.7) than the mailbox matches. You may want to spot-check them.\n3. I didn't assert authority for `sku/code`, `supplier/code` or the factory-sourced attributes, because no single system owns them.",
