   "final": "All three folders are ingested: 135 supplier PDFs, 811 chat messages and 163 emails. The store now holds 422 documents with facts, each dated by issue time, and the write ran with no errors.\n\n**What I read**\n\n| Kind | Read | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Proforma invoices | 48 | Every line total matches the printed total |\n| Commercial invoices and packing lists | 41 | |\n| Inspection reports | 46 | |\n| Chat messages | 124 of 811 | The rest are small talk, stickers, photos and voice notes |\n| Forwarder emails | 104 | 32 bookings, 4 rolls, 31 pre-alerts, 30 arrival notices, 7 ETA updates |\n| Warehouse emails | 29 | |\n| Broker emails | 30 | |\n\nNothing was skipped as already read. The catalogue had cited the PIs and invoices, but only for item codes.\n\n**What changed in the store**\n- **Purchase orders:** 48 are now in it. 26 existed as bare entries and 22 are new.\n- **Shipments:** 32, covering 31 house bills and one booking that hasn't sailed.\n- **Merged identifiers:** 31 shipments carry both a booking number and a house bill. A booking was never turned into a second shipment, including the six consolidated containers shared by several suppliers.\n- **Other entities:** 196 PO lines, 166 shipment lines, 46 inspections and 30 customs entries.\n- **PO statuses:**\n  - 37 received\n  - 4 shipped\n  - 1 ready\n  - 5 in production\n  - 1 confirmed\n- **Chat timestamps:** I read them as New York time, with daylight saving applied.\n- **Open shipments:** PBLHB2600030 has arrived and PBLHB2600031 is at sea.\n\n**Facts written below confidence 1**\n- **0.9, 76 facts:**\n  - ETD slips named by PO number, with the year inferred as the next occurrence of that date.\n  - Container numbers from chat, where the PO is named only by context. They all agreed with the later invoices.\n  - Deposit acknowledgements, where the PO is inferred from the preceding deposit message.\n- **0.85, 6 facts:** ETD slips where the supplier named a PI number, which I mapped to its PO.\n- **0.8:** a \"\u5927\u8d27\u751f\u4ea7\u4e2d\" (production under way) status, where only one PO was a candidate.\n\n**Not in the vocabulary**\n- **Chat items:** price rises and rebates, holiday closures, deposit and balance payments, sample couriers (DHL AWBs), quote and catalogue requests. There are 55 such messages.\n- **Booking PO lists:** a booking's PO list has no attribute, so POs are only linked to a shipment through shipment lines. 22 loosely written names (\"PO144\", \"po 0147\") were read as full PO numbers.\n- **Warehouse discrepancies:** 21 receipts had damage, plus short receipts such as 1,656 of 1,680 on `PBLHB2500005` and 552 of 576 on `TGHU7372239`.\n- **\"Sent\" status:** I did not assert `sent` when a PO was sent by chat, because the skill's status table doesn't prescribe it.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Early arrivals:** arrival notices are dated before the arrival date they give, so shipments show `arrived` a day or two early, as the skill specifies.\n- **Inspector name:** the reports print \"LINKCHECK INSPECTION SERVICES\", so I wrote \"Linkcheck Inspection Services\". The agency's own capitalisation is unknown.\n- **Email hashes:** I hashed each email from its `From ` line up to, but not including, the blank separator line.\n- **No conflicts:** I found no HS code mismatches, quantity or price differences, or container conflicts. No item code lacked a SKU and no B/L failed to match a shipment.\n\nThe scripts are in the scratchpad directory (`parse.py`, `build.py`, `write.py`), so the run can be repeated or audited.",
